IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Sale of Food Act 1973 (Singapore) -- whether what I sell is food and whether I am selling it, whether I run a food business
-- that needs a licence, which Part 3 offences my sale commits, the defences open to me, what may be done to me after a seizure or
-- a direction, my appeals and their deadlines, and the most I can be fined.
--
-- SEAT: the person who sells or handles food -- a food seller, including one who carries on a food business (a hawker, a caterer,
-- a central kitchen, an importer or a wholesaler) and is the person the Act's prohibitions and penalties are applied to.
--
-- Provisions covered: s 2 ("handling", "proprietor"); ss 2A(1), (3), (4); 2B; 2C(1), (2); 2D(1), (2)(b); 2E(1), (2), (3)(b);
-- 2F(1); s 4(1)(e), (2), (4); s 10I(4), (5), (6); s 10K; ss 11 to 15, 16(1), 16A(6), (7), 17 to 21; s 24(1); s 25; s 30(1);
-- ss 31, 32, 33(1) to (3); s 34(1); s 40(3); s 41(3); s 45(1); s 46(6), (9), (12), (14); ss 48(3), 49, 50(1).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, version in force from 1 May 2026 (SSO "Current version as at 01 Oct
-- 2026"), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/SFA1973.txt.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the Director-General, officers and analysts and their appointment (s 3); the inspection, information and sampling
-- powers beyond the offences of refusing them (ss 4(1)(a) to (d), (f), (g), 5 to 8, 10); what each Part 2A direction may contain
-- (ss 10A to 10H) and s 10L; the infectious-disease and vehicle rules (ss 22, 23) beyond the general offence; the presumptions in
-- ss 2E(3)(a), (c) to (e), 16A(4), (5), 26 to 28; analysts' certificates, non-disclosure, costs, fees and the appeal to the High
-- Court (ss 34(2), (3), 36 to 39); s 40(1), (2) and (4), (5); forfeiture, publication of convictions, service (ss 42 to 44);
-- licence grant, security and transfer (s 46(1) to (5), (7), (8), (10), (11), (13), (15), (16)); ss 47, 51 to 56. No food
-- regulations or orders were deposited, so what they prescribe (prohibited substances, permitted proportions, labelling and
-- advertising requirements, standards, licence fees, the appeal period under s 10J, which offences are compoundable, the penalties
-- for regulation offences) is asked as a fact or answered NOTHING, as each decision says.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the individual's seat, with
-- the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. NOT FOR PUBLIC
-- USE AS ADVICE. See NOTES.md.

§ `Sale of Food Act 1973 -- the food seller`

§§ `s 2A -- is what I sell food`

-- s 2A(1): "food" includes (a) "any substance or thing of a kind used, capable of being used, or represented as being for use, for
-- human consumption (whether it is live, raw, prepared or partly prepared)"; (b) ingredients and additives; (d) chewing gum;
-- (e) anything the Minister declares food by order. (2) includes drinking water, milk, meat, fish, eggs, raw fruit and vegetables.
-- (3) "However, food does not include" (a) a health product; (b) a medicinal product; (c) a controlled drug or psychoactive
-- substance; (d) a poison; (e) cosmetics; (f) "any tobacco product or tobacco substitute"; (g) "any package (except edible
-- packaging)"; (h) "any fodder or feeding stuffs for animals"; (i) anything declared by order not to be food.
-- (4): it is food "regardless of whether or not it is in a condition fit for human consumption". (5): "food" may include live
-- animals and plants.
DECLARE `What the article is` IS ONE OF
    `something people eat or drink`                    -- s 2A(1)(a), (2)
    `an ingredient or additive`                        -- s 2A(1)(b)
    `chewing gum`                                      -- s 2A(1)(d)
    `a live animal or plant sold to be eaten`          -- s 2A(5)
    `edible packaging`                                 -- excepted from s 2A(3)(g); food under (1)(a) by inference
    `a health product`                                 -- s 2A(3)(a), Health Products Act 2007 (borrowed term)
    `a medicinal product`                              -- s 2A(3)(b), Medicines Act 1975 (borrowed term)
    `a controlled drug or psychoactive substance`      -- s 2A(3)(c), Misuse of Drugs Act 1973 (borrowed term)
    `a poison`                                         -- s 2A(3)(d), Poisons Act 1938 (borrowed term)
    `a cosmetic`                                       -- s 2A(3)(e)
    `a tobacco product or tobacco substitute`          -- s 2A(3)(f)
    `a package that is not edible`                     -- s 2A(3)(g)
    `animal fodder or feeding stuff`                   -- s 2A(3)(h)

DECLARE `The article` HAS
    `what it is`                                       IS A `What the article is`
    `the Minister has declared it food by order`       IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 2A(1)(e)
    `the Minister has declared it not food by order`   IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 2A(3)(i)
    `it is fit for people to eat`                      IS A BOOLEAN   -- irrelevant: s 2A(4)

-- The exclusions in (3) open with "However", so they win over (1), including over a declaration under (1)(e).
GIVEN `the article` IS A `The article`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is what I sell food` IF
        NOT `the article`'s `the Minister has declared it not food by order`
    AND NOT `excluded by s 2A(3)`
    AND (   `the article`'s `the Minister has declared it food by order`
         OR `included by s 2A(1)`)
    WHERE
        `excluded by s 2A(3)` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the article`'s `what it is`
            WHEN `a health product` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `a medicinal product` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `a controlled drug or psychoactive substance` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `a poison` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `a cosmetic` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `a tobacco product or tobacco substitute` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `a package that is not edible` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `animal fodder or feeding stuff` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE
        `included by s 2A(1)` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the article`'s `what it is`
            WHEN `something people eat or drink` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `an ingredient or additive` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `chewing gum` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `a live animal or plant sold to be eaten` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `edible packaging` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `ss 2B, 2F, 21 -- my food business, and whether it needs a licence`

-- s 2B(1): "food business" means a business, undertaking or activity that involves, in whole or part, (a) "the handling of food
-- intended for sale"; (b) "the sale of food (on the Internet or otherwise)"; or (c) "primary food production", "regardless of
-- whether ... of a commercial, charitable or community nature, or whether it involves the handling or sale of food on one occasion
-- only". (2) "However", not (a) an intermediary, part of a business other than trading in food, providing a place or services for
-- reward ("such as an Internet service provider or an auction site"); (b) one consisting "exclusively of letting for hire
-- marquees, tables, chairs and other similar furniture"; (c) one declared by order.
-- s 2F(1): "non-retail food business" means a food business (a) "not carried out for a purpose specified in the First Schedule to
-- the Environmental Public Health Act 1987" and (b) "not a primary food production business", "but includes a food business a
-- component of which is" carried out for such a purpose. The First Schedule purposes are a borrowed term, asked as a fact.
-- s 21: "A person must not carry on a non-retail food business except in accordance with a licence issued to the person by the
-- Director-General". s 24(1): contravening Part 4 is an offence.
DECLARE `Retail character` IS ONE OF
    `wholly for a First Schedule purpose of the Environmental Public Health Act`   -- a retail food business only
    `partly for such a purpose and partly not`                                     -- a mixed business: s 2F(1) "but includes"
    `not for any such purpose`

DECLARE `My activity` HAS
    `it involves handling food intended for sale`                         IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 2B(1)(a)
    `it involves selling food`                                            IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 2B(1)(b)
    `it involves primary food production`                                 IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 2B(1)(c): growing, catching
    `it only provides a place or service to food traders in a non-food business` IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 2B(2)(a)
    `it consists only of hiring out marquees, tables and chairs`          IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 2B(2)(b)
    `it is declared not a food business by order`                         IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 2B(2)(c)
    `it is charitable or happens only once`                               IS A BOOLEAN   -- irrelevant: s 2B(1)
    `its retail character`                                                IS A `Retail character`
    `I hold a licence for it and operate in accordance with it`           IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 21

GIVEN `the activity` IS A `My activity`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I carrying on a food business` IF
        (   `the activity`'s `it involves handling food intended for sale`
         OR `the activity`'s `it involves selling food`
         OR `the activity`'s `it involves primary food production`)
    AND NOT `the activity`'s `it only provides a place or service to food traders in a non-food business`
    AND NOT `the activity`'s `it consists only of hiring out marquees, tables and chairs`
    AND NOT `the activity`'s `it is declared not a food business by order`

-- READING TAKEN: read literally, the "but includes" words would sweep in every retail business, since each has a component carried
-- on for a First Schedule purpose. They are read as reaching a business that is only partly retail. The primary-production
-- exclusion in (b) is kept for such a mixed business.
GIVEN `the activity` IS A `My activity`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my business a non-retail food business` IF
        `Am I carrying on a food business` `the activity`
    AND NOT `the activity`'s `it involves primary food production`
    AND CONSIDER `the activity`'s `its retail character`
        WHEN `wholly for a First Schedule purpose of the Environmental Public Health Act` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the activity` IS A `My activity`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I hold a licence from the Director-General` IF
    `Is my business a non-retail food business` `the activity`

GIVEN `the activity` IS A `My activity`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I committing an offence by trading without a licence` IF
        `Must I hold a licence from the Director-General` `the activity`
    AND NOT `the activity`'s `I hold a licence for it and operate in accordance with it`

§§ `s 2E -- does the Act count what I do as selling`

-- s 2E(1): "sell" includes, in relation to food for human consumption, (a) bartering; (b) offering for sale; (c) possessing for
-- sale; (d) displaying for sale; (g) disposing of for valuable consideration; (i) supplying a meal to an employee under an
-- employment agreement at the place of work; (j) disposing of by raffle, lottery or game of chance; (k) offering as a prize;
-- (l) "offering or giving away for the purpose of advertisement or in furtherance of any trade or business"; (m) supplying with
-- accommodation, service or entertainment for an inclusive charge; (n) supplying food, "whether or not for consideration", to
-- hospital patients, children in care, or prisoners.
-- (2) "Despite subsection (1)", not (a) "exchanging food for food or other goods or services as part of a personal relationship
-- between individuals that is not commercial in nature"; (b) "supplying food together with accommodation to a person residing at
-- a private residence in exchange for services or labour by the person".
-- (3)(b): "food that is donated for a charitable or benevolent purpose is not to be taken to be food that was given away for the
-- purpose of advertisement or in furtherance of trade or business".
DECLARE `How I supply the food` IS ONE OF
    `selling it for money`                                       -- s 2E(1)(g)
    `bartering it`                                               -- s 2E(1)(a)
    `displaying it for sale`                                     -- s 2E(1)(d)
    `giving free samples to promote my business`                 -- s 2E(1)(l)
    `offering it as a raffle prize`                              -- s 2E(1)(j), (k)
    `serving meals to my employees under their employment agreement at work`   -- s 2E(1)(i)
    `serving meals to hospital patients free of charge`          -- s 2E(1)(n)(i)
    `donating it for a charitable purpose`                       -- s 2E(3)(b); no limb of (1) left to reach it
    `swapping it with a friend, not commercially`                -- s 2E(2)(a)
    `giving board to a live-in helper at a private home for labour`            -- s 2E(2)(b)

GIVEN `how` IS A `How I supply the food`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the Act count what I do as selling` IF
    CONSIDER `how`
    WHEN `donating it for a charitable purpose` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `swapping it with a friend, not commercially` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `giving board to a live-in helper at a private home for labour` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `ss 2C, 2D, 25 -- unsafe, unsuitable and adulterated food`

-- s 2C(1): food is unsafe "if it would be likely to cause illness or injury or other physical harm to a person who might later
-- consume it", assuming it is properly processed and consumed according to its reasonable intended use. (2): not unsafe "merely
-- because" of personal preference, moral or religious objection, harm from "inappropriate quantities", or an allergy.
-- s 2D(1): food is unsuitable if it (a) is "damaged, deteriorated or perished to an extent that affects its reasonable intended
-- use"; (b) contains or has with it a damaged, deteriorated, perished or contaminated thing to that extent; (c) is "the product of
-- a diseased animal, or an animal that has died otherwise than by slaughter", not declared safe under another Act; (d) contains
-- foreign matter "the presence of which would be unexpected and unreasonable in food prepared or packed for sale in accordance
-- with good trade practice"; (e) has packaging damaged or contaminated to that extent. (2)(b): not unsuitable merely because it
-- contains an agricultural or veterinary chemical "so long as it does not contain the chemical ... in an amount that contravenes
-- any food regulations"; (c) to (f) as for s 2C(2).
-- s 25: food "is deemed to be adulterated if" (a) it is mixed with a substance that diminishes its nutritive properties or
-- otherwise prejudices the purchaser; (b) a substance has been extracted or omitted to that effect; (c) it is mixed "with any
-- substance of lower commercial value"; (d) "it does not comply with the prescribed standard"; (e) it contains a substance
-- rendering it "injurious to health".
DECLARE `The food` HAS
    `eaten as intended it would be likely to cause illness or injury`    IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 2C(1)
    `the only objection is preference, belief, quantity or allergy`      IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 2C(2), 2D(2)(c) to (f)
    `it is damaged, deteriorated or perished so its use is affected`     IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 2D(1)(a)
    `it has a contaminated or perished thing in or with it`              IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 2D(1)(b)
    `it comes from a diseased animal or one not slaughtered`             IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 2D(1)(c), not declared safe
    `it contains foreign matter unexpected under good trade practice`    IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 2D(1)(d)
    `its packaging is damaged or contaminated so its use is affected`    IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 2D(1)(e)
    `it has a farm or veterinary chemical above the regulation limit`    IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 2D(2)(b), limit asked
    `it is mixed with something that lessens its goodness`               IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 25(a)
    `something has been taken out of it to its detriment`                IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 25(b)
    `it is mixed with something of lower commercial value`               IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 25(c)
    `it does not meet the prescribed standard`                           IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 25(d), standard asked
    `it contains something injurious to health`                          IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 25(e)
    `it contains a substance the regulations prohibit`                   IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 12, asked
    `it contains more of a substance than the regulations permit`        IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 13, asked
    `parts per million of methyl, isopropyl or denatured alcohol`        IS A NUMBER    -- s 14
    `its packaging or labelling breaks the Act's labelling requirements` IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 16(1), asked
    `it is labelled or advertised falsely or misleadingly`               IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 17: as to value, merit or safety
    `it was made, prepared, packaged or stored in insanitary conditions` IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 19; s 2 "insanitary conditions"

GIVEN `the food` IS A `The food`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the food unsafe` IF
        `the food`'s `eaten as intended it would be likely to cause illness or injury`
    AND NOT `the food`'s `the only objection is preference, belief, quantity or allergy`

-- A farm or veterinary chemical counts against the food only above the limit the food regulations set (s 2D(2)(a), (b)); it is
-- treated here as a contaminant under limb (b).
GIVEN `the food` IS A `The food`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the food unsuitable` IF
        NOT `the food`'s `the only objection is preference, belief, quantity or allergy`
    AND (   `the food`'s `it is damaged, deteriorated or perished so its use is affected`
         OR `the food`'s `it has a contaminated or perished thing in or with it`
         OR `the food`'s `it comes from a diseased animal or one not slaughtered`
         OR `the food`'s `it contains foreign matter unexpected under good trade practice`
         OR `the food`'s `its packaging is damaged or contaminated so its use is affected`
         OR `the food`'s `it has a farm or veterinary chemical above the regulation limit`)

GIVEN `the food` IS A `The food`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the food adulterated` IF
        `the food`'s `it is mixed with something that lessens its goodness`
    OR  `the food`'s `something has been taken out of it to its detriment`
    OR  `the food`'s `it is mixed with something of lower commercial value`
    OR  `the food`'s `it does not meet the prescribed standard`
    OR  `the food`'s `it contains something injurious to health`

§§ `Part 3, ss 11 to 20, 31 -- which offences my sale commits`

-- s 11: "A person must not sell any adulterated food without fully informing the purchaser at the time of the sale of the nature
-- of the adulteration." s 12: food containing a prohibited substance. s 13: "a greater proportion of any substance than is
-- permitted". s 14: "more than 50 parts of methyl alcohol, isopropyl alcohol or denatured alcohol in one million parts of the
-- food". s 15(1), (2): food "that the person knows or ought reasonably to know is unsafe" or "unsuitable"; (3) for unsuitability
-- "it is immaterial whether the food concerned is safe". s 16(1): packaging or labelling not complying with the labelling
-- requirements. s 17: labelled or advertised in a manner "false, misleading or deceptive or ... likely to create an erroneous
-- impression regarding its value, merit or safety". s 18: "to the prejudice of the purchaser any food which is not of the quality
-- or not of the nature, or not of the substance of the food demanded by the purchaser". s 19: insanitary conditions.
-- s 20: contravening any provision of Part 3 is an offence.
-- s 31: "it is not a defence that the purchaser bought any food ... for analysis or examination and therefore was not prejudiced".
DECLARE `Part 3 offence` IS ONE OF
    `s 11 adulterated food sold without telling the buyer`
    `s 12 food with a prohibited substance`
    `s 13 food with more of a substance than permitted`
    `s 14 food with more than 50 parts per million of the named alcohols`
    `s 15(1) food I knew or ought to have known was unsafe`
    `s 15(2) food I knew or ought to have known was unsuitable`
    `s 16 food not labelled as the Act requires`
    `s 17 food labelled or advertised misleadingly`
    `s 18 food not of the nature, substance or quality the buyer demanded`
    `s 19 food prepared or stored in insanitary conditions`

DECLARE `My sale` HAS
    `the food sold`                                                   IS A `The food`
    `I fully told the buyer of the adulteration at the time of sale`  IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 11
    `I knew or ought reasonably to have known it was unsafe`          IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 15(1)
    `I knew or ought reasonably to have known it was unsuitable`      IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 15(2)
    `it was not of the nature, substance or quality the buyer asked for` IS A BOOLEAN -- s 18
    `the buyer was prejudiced`                                        IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 18
    `the buyer bought it for analysis`                                IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 31

GIVEN `the sale` IS A `My sale`, `the offence` IS A `Part 3 offence`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my sale commit` `the sale` `the offence` IF
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `s 11 adulterated food sold without telling the buyer` THEN
            `Is the food adulterated` `f`
        AND NOT `the sale`'s `I fully told the buyer of the adulteration at the time of sale`
    WHEN `s 12 food with a prohibited substance` THEN `f`'s `it contains a substance the regulations prohibit`
    WHEN `s 13 food with more of a substance than permitted` THEN `f`'s `it contains more of a substance than the regulations permit`
    WHEN `s 14 food with more than 50 parts per million of the named alcohols` THEN
        `f`'s `parts per million of methyl, isopropyl or denatured alcohol` GREATER THAN 50
    WHEN `s 15(1) food I knew or ought to have known was unsafe` THEN
        `Is the food unsafe` `f` AND `the sale`'s `I knew or ought reasonably to have known it was unsafe`
    WHEN `s 15(2) food I knew or ought to have known was unsuitable` THEN
        `Is the food unsuitable` `f` AND `the sale`'s `I knew or ought reasonably to have known it was unsuitable`
    WHEN `s 16 food not labelled as the Act requires` THEN `f`'s `its packaging or labelling breaks the Act's labelling requirements`
    WHEN `s 17 food labelled or advertised misleadingly` THEN `f`'s `it is labelled or advertised falsely or misleadingly`
    WHEN `s 18 food not of the nature, substance or quality the buyer demanded` THEN
            `the sale`'s `it was not of the nature, substance or quality the buyer asked for`
        AND (`the sale`'s `the buyer was prejudiced` OR `the sale`'s `the buyer bought it for analysis`)
    WHEN `s 19 food prepared or stored in insanitary conditions` THEN
        `f`'s `it was made, prepared, packaged or stored in insanitary conditions`
    WHERE
        `f` MEANS `the sale`'s `the food sold`

`every Part 3 offence` MEANS LIST
    `s 11 adulterated food sold without telling the buyer`,
    `s 12 food with a prohibited substance`,
    `s 13 food with more of a substance than permitted`,
    `s 14 food with more than 50 parts per million of the named alcohols`,
    `s 15(1) food I knew or ought to have known was unsafe`,
    `s 15(2) food I knew or ought to have known was unsuitable`,
    `s 16 food not labelled as the Act requires`,
    `s 17 food labelled or advertised misleadingly`,
    `s 18 food not of the nature, substance or quality the buyer demanded`,
    `s 19 food prepared or stored in insanitary conditions`

GIVEN `the sale` IS A `My sale`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Part 3 offence`
DECIDE `Which Part 3 offences does my sale commit` IS
    filter (GIVEN o YIELD `Does my sale commit` `the sale` o) `every Part 3 offence`

§§ `ss 32, 33 -- the defences I can raise`

-- s 32: "In a prosecution for selling any food ... contrary to this Act, it is not a defence that the accused did not act
-- wilfully, unless the accused also proves that the accused took all reasonable steps to ascertain that the sale ... would not
-- constitute an offence under this Act."
GIVEN `I took all reasonable steps to check the sale would not be an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is it a defence that I did not act wilfully` IF
    `I took all reasonable steps to check the sale would not be an offence`

-- s 33(1): "a good defence in any prosecution for an offence under Part 3 if the accused proves that" (a) the accused bought the
-- food "in reliance on a written warranty or other written statement as to the nature of the food", signed by or for the seller;
-- (b) "had no reason to believe" the food did not conform; (c) had it conformed, the sale "would not have constituted the offence
-- charged". (2): a warranty by "a person resident outside Singapore" is no defence unless the accused "had taken reasonable steps
-- to ascertain and did in fact believe in the truth" of it. (3): no defence unless "within 7 days after service of the summons"
-- the accused delivered to the prosecutor a copy with a written notice naming the warrantor, "and has also within the same time
-- sent by registered post a like notice" to the warrantor.
-- READING TAKEN: "within 7 days after service" is counted from the day after service, so the last day is the service day + 7.
DECLARE `My warranty` HAS
    `I am charged with a Part 3 offence`                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `I bought the food relying on a written warranty signed for my seller`  IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 33(1)(a)
    `I had no reason to believe the food did not match it`                  IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 33(1)(b)
    `the sale would not have been the offence had the food matched it`      IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 33(1)(c)
    `the warrantor resides outside Singapore`                               IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 33(2)
    `I took reasonable steps to check it and did believe it`                IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 33(2)
    `the day the summons was served on me`                                  IS A DATE      -- s 33(3)
    `the day both notices were delivered and posted`                        IS A DATE      -- s 33(3): prosecutor and warrantor

GIVEN `the warranty` IS A `My warranty`
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must I give notice that I rely on the warranty` IS
    `the warranty`'s `the day the summons was served on me` PLUS 7

GIVEN `the warranty` IS A `My warranty`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I rely on my supplier's warranty as a defence` IF
        `the warranty`'s `I am charged with a Part 3 offence`
    AND `the warranty`'s `I bought the food relying on a written warranty signed for my seller`
    AND `the warranty`'s `I had no reason to believe the food did not match it`
    AND `the warranty`'s `the sale would not have been the offence had the food matched it`
    AND (   NOT `the warranty`'s `the warrantor resides outside Singapore`
         OR `the warranty`'s `I took reasonable steps to check it and did believe it`)
    AND `the warranty`'s `the day both notices were delivered and posted`
            AT MOST `By when must I give notice that I rely on the warranty` `the warranty`

-- s 16A(6): it is a defence to an advertising charge to prove (a) the accused was in the business of transmitting communications,
-- with "no control over the nature or content", or (b) carried on the business of publishing advertisements and published this
-- one "in the ordinary course of that business". (7): "However, subsection (6) does not apply if the accused" (a) "ought
-- reasonably to have known" publication was an offence; (b) had been told in writing by or for the Director-General; or (c) "is
-- the proprietor of a food business or is otherwise engaged in the conduct of a food business for which the advertisements
-- concerned were published".
DECLARE `My advertisement charge` HAS
    `I only transmit communications and have no control over their content`  IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 16A(6)(a)
    `I publish advertisements and published this one in the ordinary course` IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 16A(6)(b)
    `I ought reasonably to have known publishing it was an offence`          IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 16A(7)(a)
    `the Director-General had told me in writing it would be an offence`     IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 16A(7)(b)
    `I run or work in the food business the advertisement was for`           IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 16A(7)(c)

GIVEN `the charge` IS A `My advertisement charge`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I use the publisher's defence for the advertisement` IF
        (   `the charge`'s `I only transmit communications and have no control over their content`
         OR `the charge`'s `I publish advertisements and published this one in the ordinary course`)
    AND NOT `the charge`'s `I ought reasonably to have known publishing it was an offence`
    AND NOT `the charge`'s `the Director-General had told me in writing it would be an offence`
    AND NOT `the charge`'s `I run or work in the food business the advertisement was for`

§§ `ss 4, 10I, 10K -- seizures and directions`

-- s 4(2): "Any person claiming anything seized under this section may within 48 hours after the seizure complain thereof to a
-- Magistrate's Court", which may confirm or disallow the seizure and order the article restored. (3): with no complaint in 48
-- hours, or if confirmed, the article "becomes the property of the Agency" and must be destroyed or disposed of.
-- s 4(4): where the seizure is made under (1)(e) (food that "is or appears to be unwholesome or deleterious to health" or not
-- compliant), the officer "has to immediately give written notice of the seizure" to the owner, consignor, consignee or agent, "if
-- the name and address ... are attached to that food ... or are otherwise known to the authorised officer and the address is in
-- Singapore".
GIVEN `hours since the seizure` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I still complain to a Magistrate's Court about the seizure` IF
    `hours since the seizure` AT MOST 48

GIVEN `seized as unwholesome or non-compliant food under s 4(1)(e)` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `my name and address are on the food or known to the officer` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `my address is in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I be given written notice of the seizure at once` IF
        `seized as unwholesome or non-compliant food under s 4(1)(e)`
    AND `my name and address are on the food or known to the officer`
    AND `my address is in Singapore`

-- s 10K(1): "A person to whom a direction under this Part is addressed must not, without reasonable excuse" (a) carry on an
-- activity in contravention of it; (b) "neglect or refuse to comply"; (c) fail to comply with a condition of it. (2) $10,000 or
-- 12 months or both. (3): "A person must not remove the copy of any direction affixed to any food premises under section
-- 10C(1)(c) while that direction remains in force." (4) $5,000 or 6 months or both.
-- s 10B(5): a direction continues in force until its stated expiry date or until the Director-General revokes it.
DECLARE `The direction` HAS
    `it is addressed to me`                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `I carried on an activity it forbids`                       IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 10K(1)(a)
    `I neglected or refused to comply with it`                  IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 10K(1)(b)
    `I failed to meet a condition in it`                        IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 10K(1)(c)
    `I had a reasonable excuse`                                 IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 10K(1)
    `I removed its copy affixed to food premises`               IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 10K(3)
    `it was in force when I removed it`                         IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 10K(3), s 10B(5)
    `days the direction gives me to comply`                     IS A NUMBER    -- set by the direction, not the Act

GIVEN `the direction` IS A `The direction`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I committing an offence by not complying with the direction` IF
        `the direction`'s `it is addressed to me`
    AND (   `the direction`'s `I carried on an activity it forbids`
         OR `the direction`'s `I neglected or refused to comply with it`
         OR `the direction`'s `I failed to meet a condition in it`)
    AND NOT `the direction`'s `I had a reasonable excuse`

-- s 10K(3) names no excuse and no addressee: "A person".
GIVEN `the direction` IS A `The direction`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I committing an offence by removing the posted direction` IF
        `the direction`'s `I removed its copy affixed to food premises`
    AND `the direction`'s `it was in force when I removed it`

-- The s 10K(1) duty as a regulative rule. The time to comply is whatever the direction itself allows.
DECLARE `Party to a direction` IS ONE OF `the person to whom the direction is addressed`
DECLARE `Step under a direction` IS ONE OF `comply with the direction and its conditions`

GIVEN `the direction` IS A `The direction`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party to a direction` `Step under a direction`
DECIDE `my duty to comply with the direction` IS
    PARTY `the person to whom the direction is addressed`
    MUST `comply with the direction and its conditions`
    WITHIN `the direction`'s `days the direction gives me to comply`
    LEST BREACH BY `the person to whom the direction is addressed`

-- s 10I(1): a person bound by a direction who suffers loss may apply to the Agency for compensation "if the person considers that
-- there were insufficient grounds". (2): "If there were insufficient grounds", the Agency "is to pay just and reasonable
-- compensation". (4): not determined "within 28 days after receiving the application" -- "taken to have refused". (5): review by
-- the District Court (a) "within 14 days after the day on which notification of the determination was received"; or (b) in a
-- deemed refusal, "within 14 days after the 28-day period ... ends". (6): above the District Court's jurisdictional limit, to the
-- General Division of the High Court. The limit is set outside this Act and is asked.
GIVEN `the Agency determined my application within 28 days` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the day I received the Agency's notification` IS A DATE,
      `the day the Agency received my application` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must I apply to court to review the compensation decision` IS
    IF `the Agency determined my application within 28 days`
    THEN `the day I received the Agency's notification` PLUS 14
    ELSE `the day the Agency received my application` PLUS 28 PLUS 14

DECLARE `Review court` IS ONE OF `the District Court`, `the General Division of the High Court`

GIVEN `the compensation I seek is above the District Court's limit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Review court`
DECIDE `Which court reviews the compensation decision` IS
    IF `the compensation I seek is above the District Court's limit`
    THEN `the General Division of the High Court`
    ELSE `the District Court`

§§ `ss 45, 46 -- my licence, and appealing to the Minister`

-- s 45(1): "Subject to sections 10J and 46(14), any person who is aggrieved by any notice, order or decision of the
-- Director-General may, within 7 days of the notice, order or decision, appeal in writing to the Minister whereupon the execution
-- of the notice, order or decision must be stayed."
-- s 46(14): an appeal against (a) refusal to grant or renew a licence, (b) suspension or cancellation, (c) a financial penalty, or
-- (d) forfeiture of a deposit or bond lies to the Minister "within 14 days". It says nothing of a stay.
-- s 10J(2): an appeal against a Part 2A direction must be made "within a prescribed period after the date of receipt"; no
-- regulations were deposited, so the period is not known here: NOTHING.
-- READING TAKEN: "within 7 days of" and "within 14 days of" are counted from the day after, so the last day is the date + 7 or + 14.
DECLARE `What I want to appeal` IS ONE OF
    `the refusal to grant or renew my licence`
    `the suspension or cancellation of my licence`
    `a financial penalty on my licence`
    `the forfeiture of my deposit or bond`
    `a Part 2A direction`
    `another notice, order or decision of the Director-General`

GIVEN `what` IS A `What I want to appeal`, `the date of the decision` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `What is the last day I can appeal to the Minister` IS
    CONSIDER `what`
    WHEN `a Part 2A direction` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `another notice, order or decision of the Director-General` THEN JUST (`the date of the decision` PLUS 7)
    OTHERWISE JUST (`the date of the decision` PLUS 14)

GIVEN `what` IS A `What I want to appeal`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my appeal stay the decision` IF
    CONSIDER `what`
    WHEN `another notice, order or decision of the Director-General` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 46(12): where a licensee (a) "is in breach of any restriction or condition subject to which the licence was granted"; or
-- (b) "fails to comply with an applicable requirement of this Act, the non-compliance with which is not an offence", the
-- Director-General may (c) suspend or cancel the licence; and (d) "in the case of paragraph (a)" impose a financial penalty "not
-- exceeding $5,000".
DECLARE `My licence lapse` IS ONE OF
    `I breached a condition or restriction of my licence`
    `I failed a requirement whose breach is not an offence`

GIVEN `the lapse` IS A `My licence lapse`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the largest financial penalty on my licence` IS
    CONSIDER `the lapse`
    WHEN `I breached a condition or restriction of my licence` THEN 5000
    WHEN `I failed a requirement whose breach is not an offence` THEN 0

-- s 46(9): "Where a licence is granted for less than 12 months, the Director-General may charge a proportionate fee therefor; and
-- in charging such proportionate fee, any part of a month is to be reckoned as one month." The fee itself is prescribed (s 46(8))
-- and none was deposited, so the annual fee is asked. INFERENCE: "proportionate" is read as the annual fee times months over 12.
GIVEN `the prescribed annual fee` IS A NUMBER, `months the licence runs` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What fee can I be charged if the Director-General charges proportionately` IS
    IF `months the licence runs` AT LEAST 12
    THEN `the prescribed annual fee`
    ELSE (`the prescribed annual fee` TIMES (CEILING `months the licence runs`)) DIVIDED BY 12

§§ `ss 30, 34 -- the summons`

-- s 30(1): "The summons in any such proceedings must not be made returnable in less than 14 days from the date on which it is
-- served." READING TAKEN: served on day D, the earliest lawful return day is D + 14.
GIVEN `the day the summons was served` IS A DATE, `the day it is returnable` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my summons returnable too soon` IF
    `the day it is returnable` LESS THAN `the day the summons was served` PLUS 14

-- s 34(1): the analyst's certificate is sufficient evidence "unless the accused requires the authorised analyst to be called as a
-- witness, in which case the accused must give notice thereof to the prosecutor at least 3 clear days before the day on which the
-- summons is returnable". READING TAKEN: "clear days" leave out both the day of notice and the return day.
GIVEN `the day the summons is returnable` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must I ask for the analyst to be called` IS
    `the day the summons is returnable` MINUS 4

§§ `ss 24, 49, 50 and the special penalties -- what I can be made to pay`

-- s 49: an offence "for which no penalty is expressly provided" -- "a fine not exceeding $5,000 and, in the case of a second or
-- subsequent conviction, to a fine not exceeding $10,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 months or to both".
-- s 10K(2): $10,000 or 12 months or both. s 10K(4): $5,000 or 6 months or both. s 48(3): failing to give name and address, or
-- wilfully mis-stating them, "a fine not exceeding $300". Each of these three has its own penalty and no second-conviction step.
-- Offences created by food regulations under s 56(1)(r) carry whatever fine the regulation sets (within $5,000 and $500 a day);
-- none was deposited, so NOTHING.
-- s 49's "second or subsequent conviction" does not say of what; it is asked as a fact.
DECLARE `My offence` IS ONE OF
    `a Part 3 offence in selling food`                                  -- s 20
    `trading as a non-retail food business without a licence`           -- ss 21, 24(1)
    `refusing an officer information, samples or a delivery sample`     -- ss 5(4), 6(4), 7(2)
    `obstructing an officer or breaking an official seal`               -- s 41(3)
    `giving a buyer a false written warranty`                           -- s 33(5)
    `wilfully giving false information in a licence application`        -- s 46(6)
    `selling a prohibited food contact article`                         -- s 40(3)
    `not complying with a food safety direction`                        -- s 10K(2)
    `removing a posted food safety direction`                           -- s 10K(4)
    `not giving my name and address when charged`                       -- s 48(3)
    `an offence created by food regulations`                            -- s 56(1)(r)

DECLARE `Maximum punishment` HAS
    `fine in dollars`        IS A NUMBER
    `months in prison`       IS A NUMBER    -- 0: no imprisonment; where both are given, "or to both"

GIVEN `the offence` IS A `My offence`, `this is a second or subsequent conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Maximum punishment`
DECIDE `What is the most I can be punished` IS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `not complying with a food safety direction` THEN JUST (`Maximum punishment` WITH `fine in dollars` IS 10000, `months in prison` IS 12)
    WHEN `removing a posted food safety direction` THEN JUST (`Maximum punishment` WITH `fine in dollars` IS 5000, `months in prison` IS 6)
    WHEN `not giving my name and address when charged` THEN JUST (`Maximum punishment` WITH `fine in dollars` IS 300, `months in prison` IS 0)
    WHEN `an offence created by food regulations` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST `the general penalty`
    WHERE
        `the general penalty` MEANS
            IF `this is a second or subsequent conviction`
            THEN `Maximum punishment` WITH `fine in dollars` IS 10000, `months in prison` IS 3
            ELSE `Maximum punishment` WITH `fine in dollars` IS 5000, `months in prison` IS 0

-- s 50(1): the Director-General "may compound any offence under this Act as may be prescribed as being an offence that may be
-- compounded by collecting from a person reasonably suspected of having committed the offence a sum of money not exceeding
-- $1,000". (2) On payment "no further proceedings are to be taken". Which offences are prescribed is asked; NOTHING means the
-- offence cannot be compounded.
GIVEN `the regulations make my offence compoundable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be asked to pay to compound my offence` IS
    IF `the regulations make my offence compoundable` THEN JUST 1000 ELSE NOTHING
